    <string name="goals_how_title">How goals are measured</string>
    <string name="goals_how_p1">A day counts as achieved when its recorded value reaches the target. A day with no recording is never counted as achieved and is never treated as zero.</string>
    <string name="goals_how_p2">Today is unfinished, so a partial day is marked provisional and does not break a running streak. The streak counts consecutive achieved days ending today, or yesterday if today is not there yet.</string>
    <string name="goals_how_p3">Weekly goals add up the recorded days from Monday to today. When a day is missing the total is a lower bound and is labelled so.</string>
    <string name="goals_how_p4">The Recovery cut-off for a recovered day is Apex\'s own calibration choice, not a clinical limit.</string>
